{"title":"Erdos-ko rado theorem","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Theorem\">Theorem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Erdos-ko_rado_theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Theorem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that A  is a family of distinct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />-element subsets of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />- element sets with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/e/dde01f4e29da9c7bbd05e2b458ea5a21d0ee499a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge 2r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" /> and that each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> subsets share at least one element. Then the sets in A is at most;\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/1/331124f298905a64abd15d6f8f67b57edc042e16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{n-1}{r-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"66\" height=\"53\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Erdos-ko_rado_theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018083614\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU 